5: \title{An explicit graph basis and exact Jacobian certificates\\
6: for a self-dual five-form in ten dimensions}
7: \author{\texttt{uskutsav-cpu}}
8: \date{September 7, 2026}
9: \begin{document}
10: \maketitle
11: \begin{abstract}
12: We give a reproducible certificate for 81 explicit contractions of a real
13: self-dual five-form in signature $(1,9)$. The fixed selection consists of one
14: quartic, two sextic, six octic, twelve degree-ten, and sixty degree-twelve
15: polynomials. Their Jacobian has a nonzero $81\times81$ minor at four exact
16: finite-field specializations, using the same ordered functions in every
17: case. An integral coordinate convention makes each nonzero minor a
18: characteristic-zero independence witness. The construction completes the
19: functional-independence problem, with the known generic quotient dimension
20: as upper bound. It does not determine all polynomial generators or syzygies.
21: \end{abstract}
22: 
23: \section{Scope and conventions}
24: Let $F$ be an alternating five-form, with metric
25: $\eta=\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,\ldots,1)$ and Hodge convention
26: $\star F=F$. The self-dual subspace has dimension 126.
27: The literature supplies the generic quotient dimension 81 and the
28: low-degree Hilbert coefficients \cite{cederwall,hutomo}. The present
29: certificate supplies the matching lower bound using explicit graph
30: contractions. The contraction catalogs and previously discovered bases are
31: inherited from the repository's research branches; the certificate reported
32: here re-evaluates those functions at new points.
33: 
34: A graph has one vertex per copy of $F$, no loops, and valence five.
35: An edge of multiplicity $m$ contracts $m$ index pairs with inverse metrics.
36: Vertices and edges are ordered; slot order is fixed by lexicographic edge
37: order. Graph isomorphism alone does not fix the sign of an odd-form
38: contraction, so the formula identifier hashes the ordered edge record.
39: Disconnected contractions are products. The quadratic contraction vanishes
40: on this self-dual space.
41: 
42: For each increasing five-tuple $I$ containing 0, define
43: $A_I=F_I$ and let $e_I$ denote its compact alternating component vector.
44: The integral parametrization is
45: \[
46:  F(A)=\sum_{I\ni0} A_I(e_I+\star e_I).
47: \]
48: The 126 columns contain only $0,1,-1$; their components indexed by $I\ni0$
49: form an identity matrix. Every graph polynomial therefore has integer
50: coefficients in $A$, with no projector denominators.
51: 
52: \section{Fixed selection and exact witness}
53: The nine low-degree functions are those in
54: \path{results/10d_order8.json}; the next twelve come from
55: \path{results/10d_order10.json}. The first sixty selected functional
56: directions in \path{results/10d_order12.json} complete the list.
57: The remaining two degree-twelve primitive polynomial directions belong to
58: the larger homogeneous inventory and are not included in the 81-function
59: Jacobian. A dependent Jacobian row does not identify a polynomial syzygy.
60: 
